    "answer": {
      "short": "a and c; b and g; d and f; e and h.",
      "worked": "a and c: Since $Z$ is continuous, including the endpoint does not change the probability, so $P(Z\\le5)=P(Z<5)\\approx1.0000$.\n\nb and g: By symmetry, $P(Z>-1.7)=P(Z\\le1.7)\\approx0.9554$.\n\nd and f: By symmetry and the complement rule,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge2)&=P(Z\\le-2)\\\\P(Z\\ge2)&=1-P(Z\\le2)\\\\P(Z\\ge2)&\\approx1-0.9772\\\\P(Z\\ge2)&\\approx0.0228.\\end{aligned}$$\n\ne and h: Individual values have probability zero for a continuous distribution, so $P(Z=3)=P(Z=1.2)=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
